steps.description:
Design a reusable Cowork workflow that accomplishes this goal:

{{goal}}

Decompose it into the smallest set of concrete steps. For each step decide: a unique kebab-case key, a title, a standalone description (the brief the executing agent will see), which earlier steps it dependsOn (the DAG edges), and — when it clearly belongs to one function — a division (engineering, marketing, operations, design, finance, product, etc.) or a specific agent. Identify the run-time params that vary per run and reference them as {{param}} placeholders. Decide whether the pipeline is a static `dag` (fixed graph, default) or `orchestrated` (a library of candidate steps the orchestrator picks among toward a goal). Output the design as markdown: the mode, the param list, and a numbered step table (key, title, dependsOn, division/agent).
